{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"inglorious-hermitical-lowchen","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe current tests inspect replacement mechanics or final JSON rather than the write window (`test_applier_mapping.py:235-282`, `test_applier_provenance.py:155-185`), permit last-writer record loss (`test_bridge_state_atomic_write_concurrency.py:41-120`), and source-grep impossible-link durability (`test_impossible_links_cicada.py:467-493`). Live sidecars replace full snapshots in `peer_confirmations.py:192-217` and `impossible_links.py:376-401`.\n\n## Approach\n\nUse the existing locked store boundary for read-merge-write. Preserve distinct keys under concurrent writers, choose and document deterministic same-key resolution, and prove readers see either the old complete document or the new complete document. Verify real commit-back through a fresh store/read rather than source inspection.\n\n## Scope\n\n- reconciliation mapping, peer-confirmation, and impossible-link sidecar writers\n- atomic persistence helpers\n- focused concurrency, mapping, provenance, and durability tests\n\n## Testing\n\nUse barriers for two writers and an in-window reader; cover distinct keys, same key, malformed intermediate data, commit-back, and a fresh-reader control.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Concurrent writes for distinct sidecar keys retain both records.\n- [ ] Same-key conflict resolution is deterministic and covered by an explicit test.\n- [ ] A barrier reader observes only the complete old or complete new state, never partial JSON.\n- [ ] Mapping, peer-confirmation, and impossible-link writes use the common locked read-merge-write path.\n- [ ] A fresh store/read proves committed impossible-link and mapping state survives publication.","id":"38ab-928f-edf3-4d0b","parent_id":"78f2-b104-e3c9-4b86","priority":1,"tags":["janitor","reconciler","concurrency","rp16"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"Make reconciliation sidecar persistence conflict-safe and observationally proven"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788313621839043001,"uuid":"edd0b551-ad4a-47fb-892d-09788aa57ade"}